Subject: Diagnostic: rollback network matches predict the inputs on their way
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Rollback study, after tweak patch 0029. Network matches with rollback
(RECHARGED_ROLLBACK): the network router lets the port decide whether a step
can run (HasInput) and apply its inputs (OnInputReady), so that a step whose
inputs have not arrived from another machine runs with that machine's last
inputs, and goes back when they arrive and differ. The router's queue limit
is the port's, fixed for the match on every machine; each step's inputs
leave as soon as they are captured (one tick per packet); a step undone and
run again does not capture and send its inputs a second time
(NetworkInputManager::CaptureInputs), which also leaves a capture out, or
sends the same inputs again, when the port shortens or lengthens this
machine's input delay by a step (the other machines apply its messages one
per step, in order); and the sync data an input message carries is the
checksum of the last step whose inputs had all arrived, which the port
compares with the other machines' (the state now may rest on predicted
inputs); every other message carries instead the frame word alone (flag 2,
which the original never sets), with the port's measure for its time sync.

Add include/mscharged_rollback_netplay.h, its interface to the port.

Without RECHARGED_ROLLBACK nothing changes.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_rollback_netplay.h b/include/mscharged_rollback_netplay.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a2aaa87
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/mscharged_rollback_netplay.h
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#ifndef MSCHARGED_ROLLBACK_NETPLAY_H
+#define MSCHARGED_ROLLBACK_NETPLAY_H
+
+// Network matches with rollback (RECHARGED_ROLLBACK; the port's
+// src/platform/rollback_netplay.cpp): the network router lets the port decide
+// whether a step can run and apply its inputs.
+#include "mscharged_rollback.h"
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+// Whether this match predicts: the inputs of machines that have not arrived
+// yet are predicted, and a later frame goes back when they differ.
+bool mscharged_rollback_predicting(void);
+// At the router's reset for a match: the steps of input delay every machine
+// uses (the router's queue limit, fixed while the match lasts).
+int mscharged_rollback_network_reset(void);
+// Whether the next step can run, in place of the router's queues.
+bool mscharged_rollback_has_input(void);
+// Applies the next step's inputs, in place of the router.
+void mscharged_rollback_input_ready(void);
+// Whether the local inputs are still to be captured and sent for this step:
+// a step undone and run again sent them the first time, and a capture left
+// out shortens this machine's input delay by a step.
+bool mscharged_rollback_can_capture(void);
+// After a capture: how many more messages to send with the same inputs, each
+// lengthening this machine's input delay by a step.
+int mscharged_rollback_extra_captures(void);
+// What an outgoing input message carries besides the inputs: 1, sync data
+// (the last step whose inputs all arrived, with its checksum and random
+// seed); 2, a frame word only (`frame`: how far ahead of this machine the
+// others' inputs come, for the time sync); 0, neither.
+int mscharged_rollback_sync_data(unsigned* checksum, unsigned* frame, unsigned* seed);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+
+#endif // MSCHARGED_ROLLBACK_NETPLAY_H
+#endif // MSCHARGED_TWEAKS
